    {
      "id": "8cm56cy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke discovered cells in 1665 by examining cork, while Anton von Leeuwenhoek first observed living cells.",
        "Schleiden and Schwann formulated Cell Theory, later expanded by Rudolf Virchow with the concept 'Omnis cellula-e-cellula'.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack membrane-bound organelles and a true nucleus, whereas eukaryotic cells possess a well-defined nucleus.",
        "The cell membrane is a selectively permeable lipid bilayer best described by Singer and Nicolson's Fluid Mosaic Model.",
        "Plant cells contain cell walls, plastids, and large central vacuoles, which are absent or distinct in animal cells."
      ],
      "id": "ky5gefr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t5pxyps",
      "content": "• Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 while observing cork under a microscope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iz8g6yh",
      "content": "• He described the small compartments as 'cells'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ot15rkc",
      "content": "• Anton van Leeuwenhoek later observed living cells using a microscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "3qa9q12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Cell Theory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6761wzz",
      "content": "• All living organisms are composed of cells."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g87kt80",
      "content": "• The cell is the basic unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b4cd07v",
      "content": "• All cells arise from pre-existing cells."
    },
    {
